  "content": "# Full context and every ask given\n\n**Subject:** Paul Cushman (`paul@opulent.ai`) — fractional CRO; attending Climate Week NYC 2026 (20–27 Sep).  \n**Operator:** Jeremy Alston, directing work onto Paul’s Opulent account.  \n**This file is the human + agent ask trail.** Briefs actually submitted to production agents are in `asks-submitted/`.\n\n---\n\n## Who Paul is (operator facts, as specified)\n\n- Going **to NY Climate Tech Week** (attendance is a fact, not a maybe).\n- **Fractional CRO** to **seed-ish** startups (funded Seed / pre-Series A).\n- Typical buyer: **20–50 people**, **founder-led sales** *or* a **sales manager/director ~10 years** who needs operating help.\n- **Primarily SaaS, data, and AI-driven.** Climate tech is **experience he has**, **not the only focus**.\n- Geography preference: **Midwest / Chicago gravity** for CRO clients. Climate Week is NYC for networking.\n- Motion: **warm introductions** through the network, not cold spray. Named anchors: **Chicago Ventures, GTM Ventures, GTM Fund**. “**Lexus Ventures**” spelling was never confirmed.\n- Offer includes **voice & persona training**, CRM/database systemization, pipeline process.\n- **Two climate-risk data providers** were called out as a niche (later mapped to Jupiter Intelligence and Climate X in existing research — not core Midwest seed clients).\n- Fragment **“N”** in the original note was never resolved. **“Climate Tech Blocker”** (Eventbrite, Luma, Luma MCP) was a named source/constraint, never fully defined.\n\nTwo jobs, not one pile:\n\n1. Pipeline of pre-Series A but funded startups that can buy fractional CRO help.\n2. Climate Week: **full spectrum of the best events, none of the best missing, only the best, fully articulated.** Qualification ≠ admission.\n\n---\n\n## Jeremy’s asks, in order (this thread)\n\n1. Keep Paul’s Climate Week **company-research** going; don’t duplicate active work.\n2. **Give me a zip of the outputs.**\n3. **Get the updated results** (company identity fix, especially Crux).\n4. **Continue** after a credit/tool interruption.\n5. Shape around the **two use cases** (CRO ICP + Climate Week). **Gemini 3.8** gathers context/intent vs outputs; **GPT-6 Astra medium** does presentation, asset development, summaries.\n6. **Continue** (Gemini paused on Gmail; skip and proceed; then Astra).\n7. **Fable 5.1 medium** go over selections and positioning and do better. **Do not allow additional searching, exploration, or asset creation** — only make what’s there better, reuse as much as possible. Paul **is going** to NY Climate Tech Week; climate is **not the only focus**.\n8. **Continue.**\n9. **Get me all the large datafiles and large lists.**\n10. **Continue.**\n11. **Continue.**\n12. **Include the full context and all of the asks we gave and how to find Paul’s account in Convex and add it to that zip.**\n\n---\n\n## What we already produced (do not redo)\n\n| Package | Contents |\n|---|---|\n| Networking (revised) | 230 screened = 99 qualified + 114 pending + 17 excluded |\n| Company research (corrected) | 24 recovered profiles → 26 scored identities; Crux Alliance ≠ Crux Climate |\n| Gemini 3.8 | Intent vs outputs: 0/26 core CRO fit; event list was vendor-prospecting shaped |\n| Astra medium | Six presentation assets + PDFs |\n| Fable 5.1 | Same six Markdown files revised in place: climate as one vertical; itinerary tiered; attendance as fact |\n\nHard corrections to keep:\n\n- Crux Climate did **not** host 7 events; Crux Alliance did.\n- Scale AI / Google / Watershed-scale / Climate X fashion matches are not participation.\n- Voltera is energy infrastructure (buyer), not climate software.\n- Event hosts/sponsors are **not** automatically CRO clients.\n- No outreach, RSVPs, ticket buys, guest lists, connector/account changes.\n\n---\n\n## Models used on Paul’s account\n\n| Pass | Route | Reasoning |\n|---|---|---|\n| Intent | `ai-gateway/google/gemini-3.8-flash` | medium |\n| Presentation | `ai-gateway/openai/gpt-6-astra` | medium |\n| Revision | `ai-gateway/anthropic/claude-fable-5.1` | medium |\n\nWorkspace for launches: `ws_1670f24ed67e4871be643bf4f6`, `executionEnvironment: \"vm\"`.\n\nSee `HOW-TO-FIND-PAUL-IN-CONVEX.md` for IDs and queries.\n"
