  "sha256": "308cd2c0ea7b2d4ca5f547ce737c216039134fc0bdc9698c1f0ec047f0d3df86",
  "content": "# Paul Cushman — intent vs outputs (Gemini 3.8)\n\nYou are running on Paul Cushman’s Opulent account. Jeremy asked you to gather **context and intent versus existing outputs**, then leave a durable brief that a GPT-6 Astra (medium) pass will turn into presentation assets and summaries. You are not that Astra pass. Do not stop at a plan. Download the attached ZIPs, extract once, and write the intent/gap package.\n\nPaul is a fractional CRO. Two jobs, not one blended research pile.\n\n## Use case 1 — GTM / fractional CRO services\n\nFind **pre-Series A but funded** startups Paul can offer CRO services to.\n\nShaping constraints (keep these separate; do not OR them into one mushy ICP):\n\n1. Early-stage tech, **founder-led sales**, need systematic databases/CRM/process.\n2. **Seed-stage** company.\n3. **20–50 people, no salespeople**.\n4. Or a **sales manager / sales director with ~10 years** who needs operating help.\n5. Fragment in the source note: “N” — treat as unresolved; do not invent what N meant.\n6. **Geography preference: Midwest** (Chicago gravity). Not NYC-only, not coastal-default.\n7. **Primarily SaaS, data, and AI-driven.**\n8. **Two climate-risk data providers** are in-scope as a niche, not the whole market.\n9. There are other software/SaaS niches; name them only with evidence.\n10. **Warm introductions through the network**, not cold spray. Named network anchors: Lexus Ventures, GTM Ventures, Chicago Ventures, GTM Fund.\n11. **Voice & persona training** is part of the GTM motion he sells/needs, not a Climate Week event filter.\n\nICP is buyers of fractional CRO help. Climate Week hosts/sponsors/speakers are **not** automatically CRO clients. A 14k-person TIC firm, a hyperscaler, or an unfunded community host is the wrong shape.\n\n## Use case 2 — Climate Week NYC (starts 20 Sep 2026)\n\nPaul is going to Climate Week NYC and needs the **full spectrum of the best events: none of the best missing, but only the best, fully articulated**.\n\n- Official week is 20–27 Sep 2026; adjacent dates only if they are truly best-in-class.\n- Sources in play: official Climate Week inventory, Climate Tech startups he already knows, Eventbrite, Luma, Luma MCP, “Climate Tech Blocker” as a named source/constraint — investigate what that refers to from public/connected tools; do not guess a guest list.\n- Stage filter for people/companies he wants to meet around events: **Seed–A**.\n- Qualification ≠ admission. Access/waitlist/private must stay visible.\n- Do not dump 838 events. Do not hide coverage gaps.\n\nLuma is connected. Use public event tools only. No guest-list harvesting, no connector changes, no RSVPs, no ticket buys, no outreach.\n\n## What already exists (attached)\n\n`paul-climate-week-outputs-2026-09-10.zip` — networking package:\n\n- 230 screened → 99 qualified + 114 pending + 17 excluded\n- 95 core Sep 20–27 + 4 adjacent\n- top 10 ⊆ top 20 ⊆ qualified; all 99 dates known ISO\n- 32 Luma pages rechecked; 65 selected official pages unverified\n- This was curated as climate-tech **networking**, not as “best events for a Midwest fractional CRO at Seed–A”\n\n`paul-company-research-updated-2026-09-11.zip` — corrected company research:\n\n- 24 recovered profiles + Crux Alliance + Microsoft split = 26 scored identities\n- **Crux Climate did not host 7 events; Crux Alliance did.** Score 77→57 with zero verified week role\n- Scale AI / Google / Watershed-scale / Climate X fashion matches are not participation\n- Voltera 72 is an infrastructure **buyer**, not climate software\n- Jupiter Intelligence 68 is a **competitor** with 3 official hosted events\n- 480 names are status-only; original typed universe JSON was missing\n- Old 490-entity ranking is retired\n\nThose packets were built under a broader “climate software prospecting” frame. Your job is to say, with evidence, what still serves Paul’s two jobs and what does not.\n\n## Required deliverables (durable attachments)\n\n1. `intent-brief.md` — Paul’s two jobs in operator language, ICP yes/no tests, Midwest rule, Seed–A rule, network-intro rule, unresolved “N”.\n2. `outputs-vs-intent.csv` — each major existing artifact/row-class: keep / reshape / drop, and why.\n3. `usecase1-cro-fit.md` — which researched companies (if any) fit fractional-CRO clients: funded pre-A/seed, 20–50, founder-led or first sales leader, Midwest SaaS/data/AI. Explicit non-fits (UL, Salesforce, Google, Scale AI, Crux Alliance, Climate Group, libraries, etc.).\n4. `usecase2-event-shaping.md` — how the 99 qualified / top 10/20 should be reshaped for “best, fully articulated, none of the best missing” for Paul at Climate Week. Coverage gaps vs Luma/Eventbrite/official. Do not invent events you did not inspect.\n5. `open-questions.md` — only questions that change the result (what “N” is, Lexus vs other spelling, which two climate-risk data providers he already means, etc.).\n6. `astra-handoff.md` — exact instructions and file list for the GPT-6 Astra medium presentation pass: slides/one-pagers/summaries to build, what not to reopen.\n\nWrite incrementally. Cite source files. Unknown stays unknown. No outreach drafts as sendable email. No calendar/security/deploy work.\n\nModels: you are Gemini 3.8 Flash for this gathering pass. Do not switch to Astra yourself.\n"
